  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) achieves 41.1% accuracy, while config_012 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have no information on whether the profile setting (single vs. multi) meaningfully affects performance. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) directly tests whether aggregating multiple profiles improves the RNA signal, keeping the encoder (scgpt) and modality (RNA) identical to our best result. Why this is the best next experiment: With only two completed runs, the profile setting is a fundamental, unexplored design axis that will structure all subsequent multimodal experiments. If multiprofile+avgpool improves on 41%, it justifies investing further in multiprofile configurations and tells us aggregation matters. If it does not, we can safely restrict future search to singleprofile settings, dramatically reducing the effective search space. This is a clean single-dimension comparison (profile setting) from our strongest baseline, making it the most information-dense use of the next experiment under budget constraints."
}

